#!/bin/sh
#
# Refuse a commit that changes the tuned weights without updating CLAUDE.md.
#
# SETUP -- run once per clone, per machine (git config is not cloned):
#     git config core.hooksPath .githooks
# This file itself IS tracked, so edits to it reach everyone on the next pull.
# Without that one command, git looks in .git/hooks and this never runs.
#
# Why this exists: on 2026-08-30 the live score had moved 0.784838 -> 0.862111
# and no file in the repo recorded it. config/tuned.json had been edited eight
# hours after the newest saved results file, so the shipping config had never
# been evaluated into an artefact anyone could quote.
#
# This checks the one mechanically decidable half of that failure: weights
# changed, memory not updated. It cannot check whether the number you wrote is
# correct. Bypass with --no-verify when you are certain the score did not move.

staged=$(git diff --cached --name-only)

# Config untouched -- nothing to guard.
echo "$staged" | grep -q '^config/tuned\.json$' || exit 0

# Both staged -- assume the author did the work.
echo "$staged" | grep -q '^CLAUDE\.md$' && exit 0

cat >&2 <<'EOF'

  config/tuned.json is staged, but CLAUDE.md is not.

  The score has probably moved. Before committing:

    1. Run the evaluator against the new config:
         $env:SHOPPING_COPILOT_CONFIG = "config\tuned.json"
         python -m evaluator.local_evaluator --output c:\tmp\out.json
       (--output to scratch, NEVER results.json)

    2. Update the "Current state" table in CLAUDE.md with the measured
       TechnicalScore, and add a dated entry under "What was found" saying
       what changed and why.

  Certain the score did not change? Commit again with --no-verify.

EOF
exit 1
